Source: argus
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: argus
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gawk, gnuplot-nox
Suggests: fail2ban, crowdsec, jq
Description: SSH attack counter and historical chart, no dependency required
 Argus counts SSH authentication attacks directly from auth.log or journald
 — no Fail2Ban, no CrowdSec, no monitoring stack required — and keeps an
 unlimited-horizon daily history in plain text files, rendered as a chart.
 .
 If Fail2Ban and/or CrowdSec are present, Argus also counts their bans per
 jail/scenario (reusing each tool's own decisions, never re-implementing
 detection) as additional series on the same chart — both can run at once.
 Never displays individual attacker IP addresses — only their daily count.
 .
 Installs under /opt/argus/, data under /srv/argus/ (world-readable, no
 sudo needed to retrieve a chart via scp/rsync), configuration under
 /etc/argus/. Two cron jobs: nightly collection, nightly chart render.
